// Verification half of the tetragon node's record_integrity lane:
// read the last 90 minutes of every tetragon ocsf class back (the
// three per-class tables via table-mode from_clickhouse — the vendor
// catch-all reconstruction — merged into one stream, because the
// per-node chain crosses classes), recompute each record's
// attestation fingerprint over the canonical serialization, and walk
// the per-node prev_event chain (chain_uid = tenzir-node-tetragon); a
// Detection Finding (2004) drops for every break — content tamper
// (fingerprint_mismatch), deletion (chain_link_mismatch), or splice —
// while the windowed walk tolerates its own edge (the first record's
// predecessor lives outside the 90m read, its link checks are
// skipped, its fingerprint recompute is not).
//
// SCHEDULED, hourly — the every wrapper, the loader-pipeline shape
// (the core node's detection-attest-verify): the first walk fires at
// pipeline start and every 1h re-walks the rolling 90m window; every
// waits for a running walk before starting the next (no concurrent
// walks against the store); restart-on-error still relaunches the
// pipeline on a hard failure.
//
// TWO legs out per break, the core lane's shape: stdout (pod-log
// visibility) and an ocsf_derive + ocsf_cast-dressed INSERT into
// ocsf.Detection_Finding with the tenzir user — the same table the
// Grafana tenzir-findings rule reads, so class 2004 + severity 4 land
// inside the rule's WHERE clauses and tamper evidence pages through
// the agent_invoke bridge. The written findings carry no attestation
// and no walked table ever reads ocsf.Detection_Finding back — this
// walk covers only the three archived classes — so the lane never
// self-feeds. While a break persists, each hourly walk re-emits its
// finding (append-only evidence) and the rule re-pages until the
// tamper is remediated.
//
// The read-back is windowed (90m) because the walk sorts the merged
// stream in memory, and this node's flood classes are the fleet's
// biggest volume: the 24h window was sized at the measured ~74 ev/s
// steady rate (a few million rows, inside the 12Gi limit), but the
// 6.20 GA bump's live measurement is ~770 ev/s — 24h there is
// ~66.5M rows x ~1KB/row catch-all round-trip, ~5.5x OVER the 12Gi
// limit, and the walker OOM-churned on it (exit 137, four restarts
// in the first post-bump hour, 14 at last check; the in-flight SELECT
// dies mid-walk, so the churn never even reaches query_log). The
// shrink math: 770 ev/s x 5400s = ~4.2M rows x ~1KB/row ~ 4.2GB
// working set against the 12Gi limit — ~3x headroom at the brief's
// 1KB/row figure (~1.5x even at a 2x engine overhead). 90m, not
// 60m: the window must OVERLAP the 1h walk cadence, not tile with
// it. At exactly 60m == cadence each event time is read by exactly
// ONE walk, and the stamping leg can land a record up to ~90s
// after that walk's SELECT snapshot (window end + 30s tolerance +
// insert latency) — its event time <= the boundary then excludes
// it from every later walk, a permanent ~90s-per-hour band where
// in-place content tamper is never caught (deletion in the band
// still falls to adjacency). The 30m overlap (90m - 1h) gives every
// record 1-2 covering walks and swallows that ~90s late-write
// budget with ~20x margin. The
// stored records come back through the catch-all reconstruction:
// ClickHouse re-sorted the JSON keys, and the operators'
// sort()-canonicalized serialization is what makes the recompute
// match what the stamping leg stamped.
every 1h {
  from_clickhouse table="ocsf.Process_Activity",
    host="clickhouse-tenzir.tenzir.svc.cluster.local",
    port=9000,
    user="tenzir",
    password=secret("clickhouse-password"),
    tls=false
  where time > now() - 90m
  merge {
    from_clickhouse table="ocsf.File_System_Activity",
      host="clickhouse-tenzir.tenzir.svc.cluster.local",
      port=9000,
      user="tenzir",
      password=secret("clickhouse-password"),
      tls=false
    where time > now() - 90m
  }
  merge {
    from_clickhouse table="ocsf.Network_Activity",
      host="clickhouse-tenzir.tenzir.svc.cluster.local",
      port=9000,
      user="tenzir",
      password=secret("clickhouse-password"),
      tls=false
    where time > now() - 90m
  }
  homelab::record_integrity::verify product="homelab-detection",
    title="Detection record chain break",
    uid_prefix="detection",
    scope_word="chain",
    windowed=true,
    link="stream"
  fork {
    to_stdout { write_json }
  }
  ocsf_derive
  ocsf_cast
  to_clickhouse table="ocsf.Detection_Finding",
    host="clickhouse-tenzir.tenzir.svc.cluster.local",
    port=9000,
    user="tenzir",
    password=secret("clickhouse-password"),
    tls=false,
    mode="append",
    max_batch_rows=65536
}
